One name cxx1 emits and cl does not: ?st@?$Tm@UP@@@@2UP@@A$guard, the once-guard for the template's static member `T Tm<T>::st = T()`, which cxx1 stores before main under a guard where cl sees a trivial P value-initialised and lays the member down as zeros with no initialiser and no guard - the same difference dynamic-init-scalar.nonames records against clang. The stored scalars gA, gD, gB, gS, gE, g, h and q are in both, under the same names, and the program prints the same on both sides.
